learn=[('Understand the context trade-off', 'A large catalog can consume context and complicate selection. Search defers schemas and discovers relevant tools, at the cost of a search round-trip. This app uses 90 real local handlers across three SDK MCP servers.'), ('Compare five environment settings', 'Run unset, true, false, auto and auto:5. The TypeScript env object spreads inherited variables and removes an inherited search override for the unset experiment. A requested value is configuration, not proof of actual activation.'), ('Observe discovery and actual execution', 'Inspect real ToolSearch requests, native tool results and completed handler calls. A tool listed at initialization is not proof that its full schema occupied the prompt or that it executed.'), ('Measure context with the real SDK', 'After each result, keep the streaming query open and call getContextUsage with detail full. Compare totalTokens and category kind used versus deferred. Catalog bytes are not tokens; post-result measurements include different conversation messages.'), ('Improve names and descriptions', 'The discovery experiment replaces query_course_notes with search_course_notes, adds detailed keywords and a searchHint. Both return the same local lesson record. One successful run does not prove a statistical accuracy improvement.'), ('Keep a critical tool loaded', 'The always-load experiment pins only catalog_status with alwaysLoad true. Other schemas remain eligible for discovery. The model then calls the status tool and the appropriate course-notes tool.')]
env='ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6\nPORT=3126\n# Windows if needed: CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe\n'
runsteps=[('Prerequisites', 'Install Node.js 24 or later, use TypeScript for this application and ensure model access plus API credit. On Windows install Git for Windows if the SDK requests Git Bash. Python is only needed to regenerate teaching HTML.', 'node --version\nnpm --version'), ('Install and create your .env file', 'From presentations, enter this application. Preserve an existing .env. Enter your own Anthropic key privately; no GitHub token or Managed Agents IDs are required.', 'cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson26-tool-search\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env'), ('Start the web application', 'Keep the terminal open. Use the exact URL printed by startup. The server loads .env through the Node startup option.', 'npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3126'), ('Compare search on and off', 'Run Search on and Search off. Inspect actual native search results, completed handlers and full context measurements. The browser comparison keeps one row per run. CLI prints the same event protocol.', 'npm run sample:env -- search-on\nnpm run sample:env -- search-off'), ('Explore default and automatic thresholds', 'Unset uses the installed runtime default; auto uses 10% and auto:5 uses 5%. Search may remain off below the threshold. Do not infer activation only from the requested setting.', 'npm run sample:env -- default\nnpm run sample:env -- auto\nnpm run sample:env -- auto-five'), ('Improve discovery and pin one critical tool', 'Run Discovery, then Critical tool. Compare metadata and actual execution. Pinning status should not force every other catalog schema upfront.', 'npm run sample:env -- discovery\nnpm run sample:env -- always-load\nnpm test')]
specs=[('Validate the experiment', 'src/config.ts', 'return { mode:', 'The host accepts a fixed classroom mode. The browser cannot supply arbitrary server commands or a replacement catalog.', 0, 1, 1), ('Create ninety catalog entries', 'src/catalog.ts', 'for (let index =', 'Three SDK servers each register thirty actual local tools. This bounded catalog teaches scale without claiming a 10,000-tool performance test.', 1, 1, 5), ('Describe tools for discovery', 'src/catalog.ts', 'const extras =', 'The discovery branch adds searchHint to the descriptive course-notes tool. The critical branch pins only the status tool using alwaysLoad.', 1, 2, 8), ('Register executable handlers', 'src/catalog.ts', 'definitions.push(', 'Each definition has a Zod input schema and a real handler. Native results come from local classroom records, not external enterprise services.', 2, 3, 6), ('Pass the search environment', 'src/config.ts', 'const env =', 'Spread the inherited environment. Remove the existing override for unset, or set true, false, auto or auto:5 for the chosen experiment.', 1, 2, 4), ('Give category guidance', 'src/agent.ts', 'systemPrompt: {', 'Append category guidance to the Claude Code preset. This describes available capabilities without embedding every tool schema in the student prompt.', 1, 2, 6), ('Apply host tool boundaries', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (input.hook_event_name', 'The PreToolUse hook records actual search calls and permits only ToolSearch and the local classroom catalog. Search changes discovery, not permission boundaries.', 2, 1, 10), ('Start one real SDK query', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run = query', 'An async input generator keeps the query alive after its first response so the host can request context usage before closing it.', 1, 2, 4), ('Observe search and tool use', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (block.type === "tool_use")', 'Record actual tool-use names and inputs. ToolSearch appearance is observed evidence; the configured environment value alone is not.', 2, 1, 4), ('Execute the matched handler', 'src/catalog.ts', 'record({ name:', 'The matched local handler records its execution and returns actual JSON content with the SEARCH-26 marker for the course record.', 2, 3, 7), ('Measure actual context usage', 'src/agent.ts', 'context = await run.getContextUsage', 'Request the full SDK measurement while the Query is still running. Used and deferred categories have different meanings; the result is not a billing total.', 1, 2, 3), ('Preserve evidence and close', 'src/agent.ts', 'const evidence: Evidence =', 'Store the configured setting, catalog size, search calls, completed handlers and measured context. Release input and close the query after observation.', 1, 1, 12), ('Render and compare measurements', 'src/client.ts', 'if (on && off)', 'Format actual Markdown and compare fresh-session context snapshots. Conversation messages differ between runs, so this is an observation rather than a controlled benchmark.', 1, 0, 10)]
document('/','Tool search. <em>Small context.</em>','Register ninety classroom tools, discover what is needed and measure actual context.','<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Register</b><p>90 local classroom tools</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Discover</b><p>Observe search and real calls</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Measure</b><p>Actual SDK context categories</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>Explore tool search at scale</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">Tool-search experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="default">Default · ENABLE_TOOL_SEARCH unset</option><option value="search-on">Search on · true</option><option value="search-off">Search off · false</option><option value="auto">Automatic · 10% threshold</option><option value="auto-five">Automatic · auto:5</option><option value="discovery">Discovery · descriptive name and searchHint</option><option value="always-load">Critical tool · alwaysLoad true</option></select><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Run tool-search experiment →</button><p class="meta">Each run starts a fresh real SDK query with 90 local read-only classroom tools. Compare search on and off first. No Slack, Jira or GitHub account is contacted.</p></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>Latest SDK-reported cost: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Requested search setting and pinned tools. Check actual events and context categories before drawing conclusions.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="configuration-panel"><h2>Actual search configuration</h2><label for="configuration-file">Configuration projection</label><select id="configuration-file"></select><pre class="json-view"><code id="configuration-content" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Only non-secret search configuration is displayed. The real .env remains private.</p></section><section class="step" id="catalog-panel"><h2>Registered classroom catalog</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="catalog" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>These are executable local training tools. The names and descriptions are the actual registration metadata.</p></section><section class="step" id="discovery-panel"><h2>Actual initialization snapshot</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="discovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Listed tool names do not prove schema loading or execution.</p></section><section class="step" id="native-panel"><h2>Actual native tool results</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="native" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Inspect ToolSearch discovery responses and actual classroom data. No response is simulated.</p></section><section class="step" id="context-panel"><h2>Actual getContextUsage measurement</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="context" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Measured after the final result with detail full. Deferred rows are outside current usage; free and buffer are not used content. This is a snapshot, not a billing-token report.</p></section><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Execution and discovery evidence</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Compare requested settings with observed ToolSearch calls and completed handlers. Automatic threshold modes may load upfront for this catalog size.</p></section><section class="step" id="comparison-panel"><h2>Compare this browser’s experiments</h2><p id="comparison">Run search on and search off to compare actual post-result context.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Catalog</th><th>Search calls</th><th>Context tokens</th><th>Deferred tokens</th><th>Completed handlers</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download redacted observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages</h2><ul id="events"></ul></section>','<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Discover tools on demand and read the actual SDK evidence.',cards(learn))
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>Only your model key is required. Keep it local and restart after edits. Existing shell variables take precedence.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>Use Node 24+, API credit and a supported model. Configure Git Bash on Windows if requested. If the port is occupied, use the printed existing-app URL or change PORT. A missing ToolSearch call in auto mode can be expected below the threshold. Review actual context categories. Measurement failure remains visible instead of being replaced with an estimate.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Install the SDK, configure your key and run the classroom comparisons.',body)
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','TypeScript host','SDK + Claude','MCP catalog','Context report']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b,count) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
xs=[170,520,870,1220,1570];svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1740" height="1600" viewBox="0 0 1740 1600"><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#087fff"/></marker></defs><rect width="1740" height="1600" fill="#f4f9ff"/><text x="40" y="52" font-family="Arial" font-size="34" fill="#101a44">Lesson 26 · Register → discover → measure tools</text>']
